# Deep Agents Loan Desk: the app, the gate and the bank. The agent has its own
# .env, in agent/ (agent/README.md).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `bun run dev` boots with every value below blank: GET /health answers
# `"status": "degraded"` and names each capability that is missing, and the
# home page says the same. Fill the REQUIRED block, run `bun run okta-setup`
# and `bun run setup-arcade <APP_PUBLIC_HOST>`, and restart `bun run dev`.
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit it.

# --- Required: you fill these ------------------------------------------------

# Arcade dashboard → your project → API keys. A project key: setup-arcade
# registers everything in the project it belongs to.
ARCADE_API_KEY=
# Your ngrok static domain, host form, no scheme: `my-app.ngrok.app`. Arcade
# calls the hooks, the loan API and the sign-in endpoints on it, and the
# browser must open the app there too: the sessions and the Arcade verifier
# live on this host only. Blank, the app runs on localhost with sign-in and
# Arcade off.
APP_PUBLIC_HOST=
#
# Nobody is seeded: users are not configured here. Add them from the terminal
# with `bun run users add`, or the demo cast with `bun run users seed-demo`,
# which prints each generated password once. Both create the person in Okta.
#
# OKTA_API_TOKEN is deliberately not in this file: it reaches `bun run
# okta-setup` and `bun run users` from the shell only, through 1Password:
#   OKTA_API_TOKEN="op://<vault>/<item>/<field>" op run -- bun run okta-setup

# --- Filled in by `bun run okta-setup`: leave blank ---------------------------
# It writes OKTA_ORG_URL only where this file has none, and replaces the three
# IDP_* values: the Okta org is their source of truth.

# Your Okta org, `https://<org>.okta.com`: where `bun run users` creates people.
OKTA_ORG_URL=
# The issuer of the org's `default` authorization server,
# `https://<org>.okta.com/oauth2/default`. Every endpoint comes from its
# discovery document, so any OIDC provider's issuer works here.
IDP_ISSUER=
# The one OIDC Web app at Okta: the app's sign-in, Arcade's hop-2 provider and
# the hop-1 User Source all use it.
IDP_CLIENT_ID=
IDP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Filled in by `bun run setup-arcade <APP_PUBLIC_HOST>`: leave blank ------
# It writes a value only where this file has none, except
# ARCADE_PROVIDER_CALLBACK, which it keeps in sync with Arcade.

# Seals the per-browser session cookie (AES-256-GCM). At least 32 characters.
SESSION_SECRET=
# The callback Arcade made for the `app-identity` provider. `bun run
# okta-setup` adds it to the Okta app's redirect URIs on its next run.
ARCADE_PROVIDER_CALLBACK=
# The bearer Arcade presents on every /hooks call. Registered with the hooks.
ARCADE_HOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=
# The bearer the approvals toolkit presents to the app. Also an Arcade tool secret.
APPROVALS_STORE_TOKEN=
# The gateway's slug: the one its dashboard form names, and the gateway
# setup-arcade looks for before it turns the hooks on.
ARCADE_GATEWAY_ID=
# `hooks`: the panel at /panel watches the live control plane. Blank, it
# replays a fixture under `next dev`, and says so on screen.
GOVERNANCE_STREAM=

# --- Optional: the defaults are right; uncomment to change -------------------
# A Slack channel id (C…) every approval request is also announced in, posted as
# the requester, with the link and no buttons: the approver decides signed in, on
# the approval page. An Arcade tool secret, uploaded by setup-arcade when set.
# Blank: the approver's DM only.
# SLACK_APPROVALS_CHANNEL=

# The app's port.
# PORT=3000
# Where the assistant column links: the Deep Agent's deployment, or its Studio.
# Blank, the column says how to start it with `mda dev`.
# AGENT_URL=
# The bearer for POST /hooks/admin/reset and /bank/admin/reset, and
# `bun run reset`. Blank, those routes do not exist.
# RESET_TOKEN=
# `off` strips act 4's free-text injection scanners, to show what they
# prevent. Blank is armed.
# INJECTION_DETECTION=
# The toolkit name as Arcade files the one deployed server (mcp/): every tool is
# LoanDesk_<Tool> on the wire.
# ARCADE_TOOLKIT=LoanDesk
# The Arcade org and project setup-arcade registers the hooks in, and looks for
# the gateway in. Blank, it takes the Arcade CLI's active ones, as `arcade whoami` shows them.
# ARCADE_ORG_ID=
# ARCADE_PROJECT_ID=
# Where tools and the gateway are, and where the verifier confirms users.
# ARCADE_API_URL=https://api.arcade.dev
# ARCADE_CLOUD_URL=https://cloud.arcade.dev
# Where setup-arcade finds or creates the User Source (the Coordinator API).
# ARCADE_COORDINATOR_URL=https://cloud.arcade.dev/api
# Pins the MCP client id hop 1 authorizes under, so a restart does not cost
# every persona another Arcade consent screen. Blank registers one per process.
# ARCADE_MCP_CLIENT_ID=
# What the app's sign-in asks for. `email` is required.
# IDP_SCOPES=openid email
# The two SQLite files, seeded from fixtures when empty.
# GOVERNANCE_DB_PATH=./governance.db
# LOANS_DB_PATH=./loans.db
# The control plane's own deadline per hook (ms), how often it re-reads the
# policy (ms), and how long an approval's grant lasts (s).
# HOOK_DEADLINE_MS=2500
# POLICY_POLL_MS=250
# GRANT_TTL_SECONDS=900
# Where the app's server-side code reads its own control plane. Blank is
# localhost:$PORT, never the public host.
# CONTROL_PLANE_HOST=
